## skills/grillme, skills/handoff

Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock
Source: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
License: MIT (full text in LICENSE-mattpocock-skills)

`grillme` is adapted from his `grill-me` and `grilling`. Upstream, `grill-me` is
a one-line stub that hands off to `grilling`, so the two only work as a pair.
Here they are one self-contained file, renamed to match the `/grillme` that
Your AI Dept.'s handouts teach. The Your AI Dept. changes, none of them
upstream: a ceiling of twelve questions per session, questions asked only where
the agent is genuinely unsure (everything else listed as an assumption),
questions asked through the agent's multiple-choice tool where it has one,
questions asked in plain English, and a closing summary of the agreed plan.

`handoff` is adapted from his `handoff`. The Your AI Dept. changes: it saves
`HANDOFF.md` in the working folder instead of the OS temp directory, and it ends
by telling the user what to type in a fresh session.

Upstream sets both to `disable-model-invocation`. Here neither is, so a request
made mid-message ("then run /grillme") still reaches them.

The upstream repo is the canonical version and gets updates first. Pull from
there if you want to track changes, and re-apply the changes above if you do.

## skills/eli5, skills/writelikeme

Copyright (c) 2026 Your AI Dept.
License: MIT (see LICENSE)

Original work. `eli5` borrows the shape of Matt Pocock's `wait-what`, a short
prompt in the user's own voice, but its text is new. The "Avoid sounding like
AI" list in `writelikeme`'s `myvoice` template is written fresh, drawing on the
patterns in Anthropic's `humanizer` skill (from the `anthropic-skills` plugin),
which earlier versions of this repository bundled verbatim.

Earlier versions also bundled `batch` (Your AI Dept.), `humanizer` (Anthropic)
and `wait-what` (Matt Pocock). Version 3.0.0 retires all three.

